# XSH free()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.free.001
anchor     functions/free.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       free(NULL) takes no action and does not change errno, and free()
           of a pointer from malloc() does not change errno either.
test       t/001-null-errno.c

assertion  XSH.free.002
anchor     functions/free.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       Freed space becomes available for further allocation: 4096 rounds of
           allocating and freeing 1 MiB all succeed (with the address space
           capped, where the system allows a cap, so that a leak shows).
note       The cap is only a way to make a leak visible; the test is also
           valid without it (it then just runs the rounds).
test       t/002-reuse.c

assertion  XSH.free.003
anchor     functions/free.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1988
says       free() accepts pointers returned by calloc(), realloc(),
           reallocarray() and aligned_alloc() as well as malloc(), and the
           allocator keeps working afterwards.
test       t/003-other-allocators.c

assertion  XSH.free.004
anchor     functions/free.html#RETURN VALUE
class      untestable
since      1988
says       free() returns no value.
reason     free() returns void; the absence of a value cannot be observed.
